<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Geremia Ghisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1251</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Geremia Ghisi was a Venetian noble who, with his brother Andrea, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinos">Tinos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykonos">Mykonos</a> around 1207 in the private Venetian ventures that followed the Fourth Crusade. The brothers held the islands as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the Duchy of the Archipelago, founding a lordship that the Ghisi family kept until 1390.</p></div>
